In this lesson, we’ll explore GraphQL subscriptions in NestJS. Subscriptions allow real-time updates to be pushed from the server to the client, which is useful for notifications, live updates, or other real-time functionality. Update the GraphQL schema: First, add a subscription definition to your app.graphql file: type Subscription {
  messageCreated: Message
}This subscription, messageCreated, will notify the client whenever a new Message is created.

